<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer said G7 dollar statement important.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer said G7 dollar statement important.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer said on Saturday the statement on the dollar issued by the Group of Seven nations was important and should be noted carefully.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer also said the G7 nations did not discuss monetary policies as these currently suit conditions.</p>
<p>The U.S. Germany, Japan, France, Italy, Canada and Britain are members of the G7.</p>
<p>--Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
</text>
